            <ArticleTitle>The Relationship Between Agar Thickness and Antimicrobial Susceptibility Testing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>503-506</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12088-017-0683-z</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Antimicrobial susceptibility testing can be done using solid or liquid-based medium. Solid-based assays are easy and inexpensive; they are limited by not being as quantitative as liquid-based assays. Agar depth can influence the accuracy of plate-based assays and it is assumed the basis of this effect is antimicrobial agent diffusion. We tested this assumption by using ETEST® to quantitate the relationship between agar depth and minimum inhibitory concentration and zone of inhibition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
